(3. WHY USE A GAUSSIAN MIXTURE MODEL?) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(The project does not begin with labeled facial-state categories. It discovers recurring) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(patterns in facial behavior. Facial behavior is continuous, and one window can partially) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(resemble more than one state.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
() Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(GMM is useful because:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(- It models each state as a Gaussian distribution in feature space.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(- It produces soft probabilities, not only a hard label.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(- It can represent clusters with different sizes, orientations and variances.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(- It gives useful ambiguity information when a window lies between states.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
() Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Before GMM, features are normalized per subject and reduced with PCA. PCA keeps 95) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(percent of variance. The system tests 2 through 8 components and diagonal or full) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(covariance models, then selects the best combination using BIC.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 10 Tf
() Tj
0 -13 Td
/F2 11 Tf
